From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:54:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: map an i386 .NET image in its WoW64 window

The window's image route refused every image flag but flat mapping and
dynamic relocation, so the COM+ flags the server sets on a .NET image
(IL-only, AnyCPU "native ready", 32-bit preferred) made it fail with
STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED. An i386 IL-only executable therefore never started
(virtual_map_main_module = 0xc00000bb), before mscoree or Wine Mono was
reached, and an i386 process could not map Wine Mono's AnyCPU assemblies.

Accept the three COM+ flags. They do not change an i386 mapping: as in
Wine's i386 loader, only a 64-bit process converts an AnyCPU image to
PE64, and the server derives the process machine from the main image
view's flags as it does for any other image.

Class: host-app
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-i386-dotnet.md
Offered-upstream: no; owner-local WoW64 VM is Playport code
---
 build/ntdll-unix/wow64_section.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_section.h b/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_section.h
index 124fe85..c5b7bec 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_section.h
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_section.h
@@ -14,9 +14,13 @@ static NTSTATUS ios_wow64_section_bounds( uintptr_t window, const void *addr, SI
     uint64_t end = owner_end, start = IOS_WOW64_NULL_GUARD;
     size_t length;
     NTSTATUS status;
+    /* A .NET image's COM+ flags do not change its i386 mapping: as in Wine's
+     * i386 loader, only a 64-bit process converts an AnyCPU image to PE64. */
     if (!image || !low || !high || !ios_wow64_valid_base( window ) ||
         image->machine != IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386 || image->is_hybrid ||
-        (image->image_flags & ~(IMAGE_FLAGS_ImageMappedFlat | IMAGE_FLAGS_ImageDynamicallyRelocated)) ||
+        (image->image_flags & ~(IMAGE_FLAGS_ImageMappedFlat | IMAGE_FLAGS_ImageDynamicallyRelocated |
+                                IMAGE_FLAGS_ComPlusNativeReady | IMAGE_FLAGS_ComPlusILOnly |
+                                IMAGE_FLAGS_ComPlusPrefer32bit)) ||
         !image->map_size ||
         image->map_size > SIZE_MAX - host_page_mask) return STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED;
     /* Wine's image mapper maps the complete image; do not imply partial views. */
